## Lore

Dramins look like ordinary humans except for ashen gray skin and small,
lidless, all-black eyes. They have no Mega-Damage hide, no supernatural
strength and no innate magic or psychic power, and nothing marks them out
for any trade.

What sets them apart is how they see the world. Nearly every Dramin is
certain that it alone truly exists, and that everything else, from rocks to
people, is an elaborate construct built around it as a test or a game. Each
works out for itself what it is meant to do and how best to do it. Some
take it spiritually and strive to prove themselves worthy of a god or an
afterlife, becoming healers, clerics, lawmen and knights-errant. Some take
it scientifically, as subjects of a vast experiment, and become tireless
problem-solvers and scholars. Others decide nothing matters and live for
pleasure, and among them are some of the most ruthless despots and
hedonists anywhere.

All of them share a sense of separation from everyone else and a calm
acceptance of the strange. They treat others as scenery or tools, form few
friendships, and seem cold, but they are dedicated, hard-working teammates
for as long as the team serves their purpose, and will walk away the moment
it no longer does.

## GM Notes

Pronounced DRAY-min. Size 5 to 6 feet (1.5 to 1.8 m); weight 110 to 190
pounds (49.9 to 86 kg). Life span 2D6+70 years, aging and reproducing much as
humans do; birth rates are very low.

Dramins travel the Megaverse by both technology and magic and turn up
anywhere; on Rifts Earth most are in North America, especially Lazlo, the
Magic Zone and the CS ''Burbs. Slave market value 1D6x1,000 credits.

Allies: none as a race, though some Dramin diplomats are dedicated
peacemakers. Enemies: individuals make personal enemies easily in pursuit of
their goals, given how dismissive they seem of others.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dramin');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dramin';

